abstract:
Braverman, Finkelberg and Nakajima introduced the generalized affine Grassmannian slices $\overline{\mathcal W}^{\lambda}_{\mu}$ and showed that they are Coulomb branches of $3d$ $\mathcal N=4$ gauge theories. We prove a conjecture of theirs that a transversal slice of $\mathcal W^{
u}_{\mu}$ in $\overline{\mathcal W}^{\lambda}_{\mu}$ is isomorphic to $\overline{\mathcal W}^{\lambda}_{
u}$. In addition, they conjecture that Coulomb branches of $3d$ $\mathcal N=4$ gauge theories have symplectic singularities, and we confirm this conjecture for generalized affine Grassmannian slices $\overline{\mathcal W}^{\lambda}_{\mu}$. Along the way we give a new proof of the smoothness of $\mathcal W^{
u}_{\mu}$, which has been previously proven by Muthiah and Weekes using different method.

We obtain local boundedness of weak solutions of double phase quasilinear parabolic equations of the form \[u_t-	ext{div} \left(|
abla u|^{p-2}
abla u+a(x,t)|
abla u|^{q-2}
abla uight)=0,\] where, we have imposed the restrictions $ rac{2N}{N+2}<p<\infty$, $0\leq a(x,t)\leq M$ is measurable and $q < p rac{N+1}{N-1}$.
